Team notifications can now be stored in PostgreSQL (galley's `postgresMigration.teamNotifications`). There is no data migration: switching to `postgresql` (or `migration-to-postgresql`, which behaves the same) drops the existing team notifications stored in Cassandra (at most 28 days old). The hourly `expire-team-notifications` pg_cron job (deleting rows with `expires_at < now()`) is scheduled by migration 20261110130000-team-notifications-ttl-cleanup.sql; pg_cron remains an external DBA prerequisite (without it the job is skipped and reads filter expired rows). Pagination matches the Cassandra reader: `has_more` is true only when strictly more notifications exist than requested (an exact fill reports `false`).
